<DocsPage title="Build & Check Pipeline" description="End-to-end flow from CLI to verified STL — scripts, artifacts, gates, and test coupons.">

<h1>Build &amp; Check Pipeline</h1>

<p>
  Every MasterTray model goes through three independent checks before it is
  considered print-ready: a <strong>build gate</strong> (does OpenSCAD produce a
  valid STL?), a <strong>manifold gate</strong> (is the mesh watertight?), and a
  <strong>slicer gate</strong> (does OrcaSlicer find empty layers or adhesion
  risks?). This page diagrams the full flow, including which artifacts are
  temporary and which persist.
</p>

