<h2>Test Coupons</h2>

<p>
  Five small mechanism coupons live in <code>STL/Test Prints/</code>.
  Because the tolerance system uses absolute millimetres (not part-scaled
  values), a 40 mm coupon validates the exact same snap clearance as a
  140 mm production box — minimal filament, faithful fit.
</p>

<table class="coupon-table">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>File</th><th>Dims (mm)</th><th>Mechanism</th><th>Parts</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>snap-outer_40x40x15.stl</code></td>
      <td>40 × 40 × 15</td>
      <td>Snap lid, over-wall (External)</td>
      <td>2 — box + lid</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>snap-inner_40x40x15.stl</code></td>
      <td>40 × 40 × 15</td>
      <td>Snap lid, inner-wall Rabbet</td>
      <td>2 — box + lid</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>slide-outer-tab_55x55x22.stl</code></td>
      <td>55 × 55 × 22</td>
      <td>Glide lid + Tab detent (≥ 55 mm required)</td>
      <td>2 — box + lid</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>threaded-jar_d35h30.stl</code></td>
      <td>Ø 35 × 30</td>
      <td>Screw-cap jar</td>
      <td>2 — jar + cap</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>jar_d55h55.stl</code></td>
      <td>Ø 55 × 55</td>
      <td>Open jar (full-size mesh stress test)</td>
      <td>1 — jar only</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Verify before printing</h3>

<pre><code>just validate-stl "STL/Test Prints"           # manifold hard gate
just check-printable-slicer "STL/Test Prints"  # empty-layer + coverage gate</code></pre>

<h3>Regeneration commands</h3>

<pre><code># Shared stress-test flags (hardware + mesh)
$HW   = "--set Nozzle_Diameter=0.6 --set Wall_Loops=2 --set Layer_Height=0.30"
$MESH = "--set mesh_hole_size=1.6 --set mesh_hole_spacing=1.6 --set mesh_pattern=Teardrop ``
         --set strut_floor_perc=0 --set strut_lid_perc=0 --set strut_wall_perc=0"

# snap-outer
python build/mastertray.py build --intent Container --lid "Snap (Outer Wall)" `
  --width 40 --length 40 --height 15 --export-format asciistl --no-report $HW $MESH `
  --out "STL/Test Prints/snap-outer_40x40x15.stl"

# snap-inner
python build/mastertray.py build --intent Container --lid "Snap (Inner Wall)" `
  --width 40 --length 40 --height 15 --export-format asciistl --no-report $HW $MESH `
  --out "STL/Test Prints/snap-inner_40x40x15.stl"

# slide-outer + tab detent  (footprint must be >= 55 mm)
python build/mastertray.py build --intent Container --lid "Slide (Outer Wall)" `
  --slide-catch "Tab Detent" `
  --width 55 --length 55 --height 22 --export-format asciistl --no-report $HW $MESH `
  --out "STL/Test Prints/slide-outer-tab_55x55x22.stl"

# threaded jar
python build/mastertray.py build --intent "Threaded Jar" `
  --width 35 --height 30 --export-format asciistl --no-report $HW $MESH `
  --out "STL/Test Prints/threaded-jar_d35h30.stl"

# open jar (full-size)
python build/mastertray.py build --intent "Jar" `
  --width 55 --height 55 --export-format asciistl --no-report $HW $MESH `
  --out "STL/Test Prints/jar_d55h55.stl"</code></pre>

<p class="note">
  The stress-test config uses <strong>0.6 mm nozzle / 2 wall loops / 0.30 mm layer / PLA</strong>
  with <strong>Teardrop mesh — 1.6 mm holes, 1.6 mm spacing, 0% strut on all surfaces</strong>.
  This stresses both hardware limits (thin walls at 0.6 mm nozzle) and mesh geometry (dense
  teardrop pattern with no solid border — worst-case for empty layers and floor adhesion).
  Loading box + lid in OrcaSlicer as a combined STL may show a false "floating cantilever" warning
  due to the interlocked shells — split into separate objects to clear it.
  See <code>STL/Test Prints/README.md</code> for the full config and what to evaluate from each print.
</p>

